hadiths[68]{hadithnumber,text}:
"540","Is'hāq narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullāh b. al-Walīd informed us, from Sufyān, from Hishām, from his father, who said: I asked 'Ā'ishah: ""What did the Prophet (peace be upon him) use to do in his house?"" She said: ""What do you do in your house?"" She said: ""What do you do in your house? He would remove his sandals, don his cloak, and sit."""
"541","'Amra reported that 'A'isha was asked, \What did the Messenger\nof Allah"
"542","Al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \When one of you has love for his brother"
"543","A man from the Companions of the Prophet met me and took hold of my shoulder from behind, saying, ""Do you not love me?"" I said, ""He who loves me loves the One I love for Him, and if the Messenger of Allah had not said, 'If a man loves a man, let him inform him that he loves him as I have informed you,' then he would have taken hold of me and said, 'Is there not a woman with you? Is she not a prostitute?'"""
"544","Anas reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him\npeace, said, \When two men have love for one another"
"545","Mu'adh ibn Jabal said, \When you have love for your brother"
"546","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \Anyone who has love for his brother in Allah\nand for Allah should say"
"547","'Iyad ibn Khalifa heard 'Ali say at Siffin, \The intellect is located\nin the heart. Mercy is located in the liver"
"548","We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when a man from the people of the desert came, wearing a garment of silk, until he stood on the head of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""Your companion has put aside every riding beast, or he said: 'He intends to put aside every riding beast and raise every shepherd.' Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) took his cloak and said: 'Do you not see the dress of one who does not have intellect?' Then he said: 'Verily, the Prophet of Allah, Noah (peace be upon him), when death approached him, said to his son: ""I am leaving you in charge of the succession, I order you to take two, and prohibit you from two: I order you to take no god but Allah, for if the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed in a scale and the seven heavens and the seven earths were placed in a scale, they would not be lifted except by the power of Allah, and if the seven heavens and the seven earths were a hollow vessel, they would not be lifted except by the power of Allah. And I prohibit you from associating with Allah and from pride."" Then I said, or it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, this is the association, we have recognized it. What is the pride?"" He said: ""No, he said: 'It is that one of us should have a cloak to wear?' He said: 'No, he said: 'It is that one of us should have a pair of good deeds, with two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good deeds, and two good d